@!internal

module nupp.runtime.bitops

--[[
The bit operations the standard library and the compiler reach by name.

It is LuaJIT's `bit`, which every target has, and this module is the one place
that says so. It had a provider interface while `--dialect lua51` lowered
`a & b` to a call on it and a scalar implementation answered where the C library
was absent; that lowering is gone, the dialect with it, and a seam with one
implementation on every target is a seam in name only.

Every operand is normalized to a signed 32-bit word first, so a wider integer
has to be split into limbs by whoever holds it.
]]

export = require("bit")
